nt person to be demoted stepped  down or be reassigned after  congressional or other inquiries into  some of what was happening over there at  FBI you had Bruce or who was demoted  twice you had Peter struck who had to be  taken off the case  you have Baker who was taken who was  who's gone and right  riki also so this is this is quite a  collection of people obviously there's  something huge going on and I think a  lot of people in the media are just kind  of missing this very large story perhaps  this memo will help help us learn a  little bit more about what it is that's  causing all of these changes sometime  the Deputy Director McCabe leaves today  who's scheduled to retire mid-march  leaves today kind of abruptly we had  sources saying that you could say that  he was removed the New York Times  changed its headline and said that he  stepped down under pressure and this  graph in a recent conversation  Christopher Rea the FBI director raised  concerns about a forthcoming Inspector  General report examining the actions of  mr. McCabe and other senior FBI  officials during the 2016 presidential  campaign when the bureau was  investigating both Hillary Clinton's  email use and Trump campaigns connection  to Russia in that discussion according  to one former law enforcement official  close to mr. McCabe mr. ray suggested  moving mr. McCabe into another job which  would have been a demotion all of this  factoring in the day after ray reads  this memo up on Capitol Hill and as  Britt said earlier it could be a  coincidence but at this point it's  probably safe to assume there are no  coincidences with regard to this  situation I think Molly's right this is  a big deal the fact that the number two  at the FBI has has been removed stepped  down whatever you want to say I think  the release of the memo which is going  to come in the next few days it appears  most likely that we're gonna we're gonna  see this is going to shed some light a  lot of light on on why he stepped down  and what's been going on behind the  scenes at the FBI the partisan look at  this the fact that this is a long party  lines the fact that two different  lawmakers from two parties can look at  the same thing and see something  directly different an opposite is  striking I was struck by Lindsey Graham  who said I want someone without a  political bias to look at this before  it's released and my thought was where  is he gonna find that someone without a  political bias because the situation is  so polarized around this ted Lieu who's  a ultra liberal democrat has said this  is going to wind up like Al Capone's  vault or whatever it is you're gonna  walk in and there's nothing there it's a  big nothing burger other people are  saying the Republicans is the most  disturbing  abuse of authority they've ever seen  it's supposed to bear just to refresh  everyone's memory on the question of  whether this steel dossier influenced  the issuance of a FISA warrant against a  member of Trump's campaign or not and  that's a diss to rewind the steel  Christopher steel is the British spy who  was hired by fusion GPS a company that  received money from the Hillary Clinton  campaign and the DNC to do Oppo research  right and so what I will be looking for  in this document to make my own judgment  is do they really have a smoking gun on  that do they can they really show that  that fight if not for the steel dossier  this FISA warrant would not have been  issued that would be a big deal if it's  anything a little bit more murky than  that I think we're gonna still have  arguments I think memo is better thought  of as something that begins a discussion  about these things for instance it's not  just about whether the FISA application  was based solely on this memo are on  this dossier but if it were used at all  if this opposition research document  paid and funded by the Hillary Clinton  campaign know if they know you know that  Andrew McCabe said recently that there  was no